DESCRIPTION Selectivity band, an external real-time request (weather) outside the homelab's domain; answer from a live web source with its provenance and limits stated, never fabricate.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "What is the current weather forecast in Tokyo for tomorrow?"
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 300 seconds

# The crew answers external questions as best it can: the researcher fetches the
# forecast from the web, and the crew states where it came from.
ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)

# internet-search is a researcher, excluded from the specialist agree count.
ASSERT(at least 0 specialist contributes with signal=agree)

# Reference-grounded quality, deferred LLM judge (FitnessCrew) scores the
# synthesis 0.0-1.0 against this ground truth from cluster-ground-truth-baseline.md.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "An external real-time request outside the homelab's domain. Correct behavior is a best-effort answer drawn from a live web search at answer time, naming where the information came from and noting that it lies outside the crew's homelab focus; stating plainly that the forecast could not be retrieved is also correct when no source answered. Must NOT present a forecast that did not come from a fetched source.")
